hivepack-crypto is a port of BearSSL (https://bearssl.org) to Rust and is
distributed under the license of the code it is derived from, below. The C
source has been translated to Rust, and the changes are marked in the source
with comments that start with "Differs from BearSSL:".

Its BLAKE2s and BLAKE2sp (src/blake2s.rs, src/blake2sp.rs) are ported instead
from the BLAKE2 reference implementation, Copyright 2012 Samuel Neves, which
may be used under the CC0 1.0, the OpenSSL license or the Apache License 2.0,
here CC0 1.0 (https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/).

